G0622.def:
ἀπ-όλλυμι and ἀπολλύω 
[in LXX for אָבַד, etc. (38 words in all)]. 
__1. Act., 
__1 to destroy utterly, destroy, kill: Mk 124, 922, al.; τ. ψνχήν, Matthieu 10:28, al.; 
__2 to lose utterly: Matthieu 10:42, al.; metaphorically, of failing to save, Jean 6:39 18:9. 
__2. Mid., 
__1 to perish; 
__(a) of things: Matthieu 5:29, Jean 6:12, Hébreux 1:11 (LXX, al.; 
__(b) of persons: Matthieu 8:26, al. Metaphorical, of loss of eternal life, Jean 3:15-16 10:28 17:12, Romains 2:12, 1 Corinthiens 8:11 15:18, 2 Pierre 3:9. In οἱ ἀπολλὺμενοι, the perishing, contrasted in 1 Corinthiens 1:18, al., with οἱ σωζόμενοι, the "perfective" force of the verb, WH. " implies the completion of the process of destruction," is illustrated (see M, Pr., 114 f.; M, Th., ii, 2:10); 
__2 to be lost: Luc 15:4 21:18. Metaphorical, on the basis of the relation between shepherd and flock, of spiritual destitution and alienation from God: Matthieu 10:6 15:24, Luc 19:10 (MM, see word; DCG, i, 191 f., ii, 76, 554; Cremer, 451)

G0649.def:
ἀπο-στέλλω, 
[in LXX very freq., almost always for שׁלח ;] 
prop., to send away, to dispatch on service; 
__1. to send with a commission, or on service; 
__(a) of persons: Christ, Matthieu 10:40; the apostles, 10:16; servants, Marc 12:2; angels, 13:27; 
__(b) of things: ὄνος, Matthieu 21:3; τὸ δρέπανον, Marc 4:29; τ. λόγον, Actes 10:36; τ. ἐπαγγελίαν (i.e. the promised Holy Spirit), Luc 24:49, Rec.; before εἰς, Matthieu 20:2, Luc 11:49, Jean 3:17; ὀπίσω, Luc 19:14; ἔμπροσθεν, Jean 3:28; πρὸ προσώπου, Matthieu 11:10; πρός, Matthieu 21:34; with ref. to sender or place of departure: ἀπό, Luc 1:26 (Rec. ὑπό); παρά, Jean 1:6; ἐκ, ib. 1:19; ὑπό, Actes 10:17 (Rec. ἀπό); before inf., Marc 3:14, al.; ἵνα, Marc 12:2, al.; εἰς (of purpose), Hébreux 1:14; without direct obj.: before πρός, Jean 5:33; λέγων, Jean 11:3; ἀποστείλας, with indic., Matthieu 2:16, Actes 7:14, Apocalypse 1:1. 
__2. to send away, dismiss: Luc 4:18, Marc 5:10 8:26 12:3 (cf. ἐξ-, συν-αποστέλλω). 
SYN.: πέμπω, the general term. ἀ. "suggests official or authoritative sending" (see Thayer, see word πέμπω; Westc., Jo., 298; Epp. Jo., 125; Cremer, 529; MM, see word).

G0694.def:
ἀργύριον, -ου, τό
(ἄργυρος), [in LXX for כֶּסֶף (Genèse 13:2, al.), exc. La 4:1 (כֶּתֶם) ;] 
prop., a piece of silver (Lft., Notes, 191); in NT, 
__(a) silver: Actes 3:6 7:16 19:19 20:33, 1 Corinthiens 3:12, 1 Pierre 1:18; 
__(b) money: Matthieu 25:18, 27, Marc 14:11, Luc 9:3 19:15, 23 22:5, Actes 8:20; 
__(with) a silver coin: p1., Matthieu 26:15 27:3-6, 9 28:12, 15, where the value is that of a shekel or tetradrachm; ἀργυρίου μυριάδες πέντε (prob. drachmas; MM, see word), Actes 19:19.†
